The attached image conceptually illustrates the dendrimer-like internal structure of phytoglycogen nanoparticles, also referred to as Nano-11 in the provided articles. These nanoparticles, derived from sweet corn kernels, are characterized by highly branched glucan chains radiating from a central core, resembling synthetic dendrimers due to their high molecular density. This unique architecture is crucial for their function as vaccine adjuvants, facilitating efficient uptake by dendritic cells and enhancing the immune response to adsorbed protein antigens, as discussed in the context of their physical characterization and immunostimulatory properties.